  "answer_text": "Here is a complete overview of the MLA and MP seats in Telangana:\n\n---\n\n## \ud83c\udfdb\ufe0f MLA Seats (State Legislature)\n\n### Legislative Assembly (Vidhan Sabha)\n- There are **119 MLAs** in the Telangana Legislative Assembly, elected by the people. The state is divided into **119 constituencies** with roughly equal populations.\n\n- The Telangana Legislative Assembly came into existence with 119 seats in **June 2014** with the formation of Telangana.\n\n### Legislative Council (Vidhan Parishad)\n- The Legislature is **bicameral**, with 119 members of the Legislative Assembly and **40 members of the Legislative Council**.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83c\udfdf\ufe0f MP Seats (Parliament)\n\n### Lok Sabha (Lower House)\n- Telangana has a total of **17 Lok Sabha constituencies**, with **12 seats** for general candidates, **3 seats** reserved for SC candidates, and **2 seats** reserved for ST candidates.\n\n### Rajya Sabha (Upper House)\n- There are currently **7 Rajya Sabha members** from Telangana.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udcca Summary Table\n\n| House | Type | Seats |\n|---|---|---|\n| Legislative Assembly (Vidhan Sabha) | State - Lower House | **119** |\n| Legislative Council (Vidhan Parishad) | State - Upper House | **40** |\n| Lok Sabha | Parliament - Lower House | **17** |\n| Rajya Sabha | Parliament - Upper House | **7** |\n\nSo in total, Telangana has **119 MLA seats** and **24 MP seats** (17 Lok Sabha + 7 Rajya Sabha).",
